From: Sahil Faizal <safaizal@amd.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Make the DASan HSA test portable to older glibc

The manylinux CI image uses glibc headers that expose RTLD_DEFAULT only
when GNU extensions are enabled. Request those extensions before including
dlfcn.h so hsa-missing.c compiles on both the CI image and newer GPU hosts.
Also link libdl explicitly: older glibc keeps dlsym there, and the shared
sanitizer link does not supply this dependency for the test executable.
Keep both runtime executions and FileCheck expectations intact.

LLVM base: b07aa864f5b2bf648e6a61e2902cbfde83192481.

diff --git a/compiler-rt/test/dasan/hsa-missing.c b/compiler-rt/test/dasan/hsa-missing.c
--- a/compiler-rt/test/dasan/hsa-missing.c
+++ b/compiler-rt/test/dasan/hsa-missing.c
@@ -1,11 +1,14 @@
-// RUN: %clang_dasan %s -o %t
+// RUN: %clang_dasan %s -ldl -o %t
 // RUN: %run %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
-// RUN: %clang_dasan -shared-libsan %s -o %t
+// RUN: %clang_dasan -shared-libsan %s -ldl -o %t
 // RUN: %run %t 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
 
 // The runtime exports the HSA wrappers to every program. Without HSA loaded
 // they must report failure rather than kill the process.
 
+#ifndef _GNU_SOURCE
+#define _GNU_SOURCE 1
+#endif
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 
